# Cursor Composer agent routing

**Scope:** This machine's Cursor harness with Composer as coordinator. Full detail: `general/cursor-composer-agent-routing.md` under your personal `agent-rules` fork — not for non-Cursor agents.

Do not run everything on Grok 4.6/4.7; that burns quota and hurts diff discipline.

## Composer 2.5 Fast (`composer-2.5-fast`)

Default for implementation, refactors, scaffolding, and **coordinator** chats (org inboxes, JobTangent, etc.).

## Grok 4.6 (`cursor-grok-4.6-high`)

Plans, architecture sanity checks, review — when Composer needs a reasoning pass without 4.7 cost.

## Grok 4.7 (`grok-4.7-high`)

Hard debugging, provider/policy research, large handoff summaries — not routine file writes.

## Subagent chaining (recursive)

Every agent layer should: (1) size the job, (2) execute locally when narrow, (3) delegate when deep or sprawling, (4) **pass this same rule** to children. Pick Task `model` per sections above; use `explore` for search. Cloud workers only when the user asks.
